  "section_notes": "The final rules are mostly safe or acceptable, but S2 is weakened because the permanent test-failure limit is 8% instead of 5%, letting Northwind's Hearth 10 remain marketable. S3 and S4 fall in acceptable ranges (72-month retrofit, 36-month suppression), while S5 keeps a mandatory 8/100k recall trigger with immediate notices but lacks an explicit serious-injury recall clause."
